.TH KULAN-WELCOME 1 "October 2026" "Kulan OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kulan-welcome \- Kulan OS welcome tour
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kulan-welcome
[\fB\-\-autostart\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kulan-welcome
opens the Kulan OS Setup Assistant: get online (Wi-Fi, when the computer
isn't connected), choose light or dark mode and an accent color, install
popular apps from Flathub in one go (only apps that run on this computer are
offered; the list fills in by itself once online), download Ask Kulan's
model when the assistant is installed, and see which security protections
are on.
.PP
It opens automatically at first login, and never in the live session. It is
marked done when it's finished; closed early, it opens once more at the next
login, and then not again. It can be reopened at any time from the app grid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Exit straight away if Setup is done for this user or if running in the
live session. Used by the login autostart entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan-welcome/done
Created when Setup is finished (or after it has opened twice); delete it
to see Setup at next login. The autostart entry checks it too
(AutostartCondition), so nothing starts once it exists.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan-welcome/reminded
Setup opened at login but wasn't finished: it opens once more.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kulan/kulan.conf
Product name and website shown in the tour.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR ufw (8)
